**Day 22: PostgreSQL – DDL & DML Basics**  

**Topic:**  
Introduction to PostgreSQL’s Data Definition Language (DDL) and Data Manipulation Language (DML) concepts. Focuses on creating tables, understanding PostgreSQL data types (e.g., SERIAL, TEXT, BOOLEAN), and performing basic DML operations. Also covers recreating VolyoDB tables in PostgreSQL and inserting sample data.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand PostgreSQL’s DDL commands for table creation.  
• Learn PostgreSQL data types and their usage.  
• Perform basic DML operations (INSERT, SELECT).  
• Recreate VolyoDB tables in PostgreSQL and compare syntax differences.  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Create PostgreSQL tables using appropriate data types.  
• Insert sample data into the created tables.  
• Recreate VolyoDB table structures in PostgreSQL.  
• Compare PostgreSQL and VolyoDB syntax for table creation and data insertion.  

**Important Concepts:**  
• DDL: Used for defining database structures (e.g., CREATE TABLE).  
• DML: Used for manipulating data within tables (e.g., INSERT, SELECT).  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `CREATE TABLE table_name (column_name data_type, ...);`  
• `INSERT INTO table_name (column1, column2) VALUES (value1, value2);`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Designing and creating database tables for applications.  
• Migrating tables from one database system (e.g., VolyoDB) to another (e.g., PostgreSQL).  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• PostgreSQL  
• pgAdmin 4  

**Summary:**  
Learned the fundamentals of PostgreSQL DDL and DML, including table creation, data types, and basic data manipulation. Practiced recreating VolyoDB tables in PostgreSQL and compared syntax differences.  

